   = note: a dash between two clauses leaves the relationship between them unstated, which is the register AI-generated prose settles into; deliberate technical writing names that relationship
   = help: do not swap the dash for `,`, `;`, `:`, `(`, `)` or `--`. Restructure the sentence so each clause stands on its own: split it into separate sentences, or pick the mark that names the relationship (a colon introduces an elaboration, a semicolon joins parallel statements, a comma attaches a dependent clause)
   = note: an assistant meeting this diagnostic in its own output is being asked to rewrite the surrounding paragraph, not to substitute another punctuation character
   = note: `#[warn(perfectionist::em_dash_prose)]` on by default

